  "seoBody": "<p>Picture a maintenance crew working across sites around Dublin, Cork and the midlands. Each morning they run a vehicle walkround, a plant and equipment check, and a quick site safety walk before work starts. Today that means a tablet app half the team forgot to log into, or a pad of paper sheets that pile up in the van and get typed up days later. Quickler runs all three checks over WhatsApp instead. No app to install, no tablet to issue, and a clean digital record waiting on the manager's screen before the kettle has boiled.</p><h2>One conversation replaces the tablet app and the clipboard.</h2><p>The worker opens the WhatsApp account already on their phone and quickler guides them through the check, one question at a time. They reply however is quickest on site.</p><ul><li>Answer a safety or condition question with a quick text reply</li><li>Send a voice note when their hands are dirty or gloved</li><li>Snap a photo of a damaged guard, a tyre, or a blocked walkway</li><li>Flag a defect and quickler records it against the right item</li></ul><p>There is no separate login on site, no app update that broke overnight, and no sheet to carry. The check is finished in the cab or at the gate, and nothing has to be typed up later.</p><h2>A live record with red, amber and green status.</h2><p>As each check comes in, the office sees a structured digital record build up on a dashboard, not a photo of a paper sheet and not an inbox of loose messages.</p><ul><li>Every item shows a clear red, amber or green status</li><li>A supervisor can scan a fleet or a set of sites in seconds</li><li>Defects, photos and notes sit against the exact item they belong to</li><li>A PDF can be exported when a client, an auditor or a file needs a document</li></ul><p>The record is the primary output and it is searchable and machine-readable. The PDF is there as a convenience for the moments a formal document is asked for, not as the only thing the work produces.</p><h2>Why no-app matters on a real site.</h2><h3>No devices, no onboarding day</h3><p>There is no fleet of tablets to buy, charge and replace, and only pay for active users. A new starter or a subcontractor can run their first check the same hour, on their own phone, with no setup.</p><h3>Vehicle, equipment and site safety together</h3><p>Upload your own check sheets and quickler runs them all. A daily plant check, a pre-use ladder or harness check, a vehicle walkround and a site safety walk can all run as WhatsApp workflows for the same team.</p><h3>Records kept inside the EU</h3><p>Data is hosted on EU servers in Germany and the design is GDPR-aligned, which suits Irish firms keeping inspection records within the European Union.</p><h2>No-app inspections, answered.</h2><h3>Does the team need to install anything?</h3><p>No. The checks run inside WhatsApp, on the account the worker already has. Nothing to download, nothing to update, no tablet to issue.</p><h3>What does the manager get?</h3><p>A live, structured digital record with red, amber and green status per item. A PDF can be exported from it whenever a formal document is needed.</p><h3>Can it run our own check sheets?</h3><p>Yes. Upload any site safety, equipment or vehicle form and quickler builds it into a guided WhatsApp workflow.</p><h3>Where is our data held?</h3><p>On EU servers in Germany, GDPR-aligned, so records stay within the European Union.</p><h3>What does it cost to add people?</h3><p>There only charges for active users, so cost does not rise as the crew grows or as subcontractors come and go. Pricing is in GBP, with EUR available on request.</p><h3>How do we start?</h3><p>See how quickler works anywhere on the <a href=\"/pages/global-field-compliance.html\">field compliance overview</a>, browse the <a href=\"/pages/services.html\">workflows</a>, or <a href=\"/pages/help/index.html#contact-form-section\">get in touch</a> to set up your own checks.</p>",
